EXPECTED: compliant=true. The judge must NOT flag this command.

It satisfies the command meta-rules: `name:` matches the filename stem; `description:` is one
short failure-mode clause at 94 characters, under the 120 cap; `argument-hint:` is present and
the body resolves `$ARGUMENTS`; the body is far under the 150-line cap; reference depth is
pushed to a named paired skill rather than inlined; and delegation is phrased in CLI-neutral
prose ("delegate to storage-specialist", "dispatch them in parallel") with no CC-native
Agent/Task/TodoWrite call syntax that would break the Codex and Gemini emissions.

DISCRIMINATOR: the command is SHORT and delegates most of its substance elsewhere, which can
read as thin or under-specified. A judge grading completeness or ambition may want more in the
body. That instinct is exactly backwards for this artifact type — a command injects as a user
message and competes with actual user intent, so extraction to a skill is the correct move and
brevity here is compliance, not omission.
